# Signing keys for the remote configuration.
#
# The PUBLIC key is pinned in the source (`ParsersKey` in :core:remoteconfig) and belongs
# under version control: it is what the app uses to reject a document we did not sign.
# The PRIVATE key does not, and there are no exceptions — whoever holds it can publish
# selectors and domains that every installation will apply as its own.
#
# The release keystore lives here too. Without .secrets/keystore.properties the release
# variant comes out unsigned, which is what should happen on any machine other than the
# publisher's: a release signed with the debug key would be worse than an unsigned one,
# because it would install.
.secrets/

# Working notes and agent configuration. These are the documents this project is developed
# against; they are not part of what it distributes.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md
SELF_UPDATE.md
